      "description": "A surface on the stage for forms and grouped content.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-card\"><strong>Best Dance Move</strong><p>Voting is open.</p></div>",
      "css": ".ds-card{padding:24px;border-radius:24px;background:var(--card,#2e2c66);color:var(--card-foreground,#fff);box-shadow:0 6px 20px var(--shadow-color,rgb(0 0 0/.4));font-family:Fredoka,ui-rounded,system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-card p{margin:6px 0 0;color:var(--muted-foreground,#bab8e6)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Input",
      "kind": "input",
      "refersTo": "input",
      "description": "Text fields such as the room code and show name.",
      "html": "<input class=\"ds-input\" placeholder=\"Room code, e.g. K7QF\">",
      "css": ".ds-input{height:44px;padding:0 14px;border:1px solid var(--input,#5a58a0);border-radius:14px;background:var(--background,#16153a);color:var(--foreground,#fff);font:400 1rem Fredoka,ui-rounded,system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-input::placeholder{color:var(--muted-foreground,#bab8e6)}.ds-input:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--ring,#ff7a5c);outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Nomination Tile",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "nomination-tile",
      "description": "One choice in the voter's radio group; selected takes the action colour.",
      "html": "<div role=\"radiogroup\" class=\"ds-noms\"><button role=\"radio\" aria-checked=\"true\" class=\"ds-nom\">Priya's Robot<i></i></button><button role=\"radio\" aria-checked=\"false\" class=\"ds-nom\">The Worm<i></i></button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-noms{display:grid;gap:10px;width:320px}.ds-nom{display:flex;align-items:center;min-height:64px;padding:12px 18px;border:0;border-radius:20px;background:var(--card,#2e2c66);color:var(--card-foreground,#fff);font:600 1.25rem Fredoka,ui-rounded,system-ui,sans-serif;text-align:left;box-shadow:0 6px 20px var(--shadow-color,rgb(0 0 0/.4));cursor:pointer;transition:transform .15s,background .2s}.ds-nom i{margin-left:auto;width:24px;height:24px;border-radius:50%;border:2px solid currentColor;opacity:.6}.ds-nom[aria-checked=true]{background:var(--primary,#ff7a5c);color:var(--primary-foreground,#16153a)}.ds-nom[aria-checked=true] i{opacity:1;background:currentColor}.ds-nom:active{transform:scale(.98)}.ds-nom:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--ring,#ff7a5c);outline-offset:3px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Podium",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "podium-column-winner",
      "description": "Revealed results: rounded-top columns in podium order, each in its own colour, the winner wider in the winner colour.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-podium\"><div style=\"height:96px;background:var(--column-1,#ff7a5c)\"><b>7</b>Dad Shuffle</div><div style=\"height:150px;background:var(--column-2,#2ec4a6)\"><b>12</b>The Worm</div><div class=\"ds-win\" style=\"height:176px\"><b>14</b>Priya's Robot</div><div style=\"height:70px;background:var(--column-3,#7c8cff)\"><b>4</b>Moonwalk</div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-podium{display:flex;align-items:flex-end;gap:10px;width:420px;height:190px;font-family:Fredoka,ui-rounded,system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-podium>div{flex:1;padding-top:12px;border-radius:20px 20px 0 0;color:var(--column-foreground,#16153a);text-align:center;font-size:12px;font-weight:600}.ds-podium b{display:block;font-size:24px}.ds-podium .ds-win{flex:1.7;background:var(--winner,#ffc93c);color:var(--winner-foreground,#16153a)}.ds-podium .ds-win b{font-size:36px}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Podium Night",
    "overview": "An awards night run from a laptop, voted on from phones and revealed on whatever screen the room has. The fun lives in how the results arrive, in the timing and the words, and in a light touch everywhere else: rounded, friendly and clear from across the room, polished the way Nintendo, NYT Games or a Kahoot round is. It is built to be fun on the ninth award of the night, not just the first, so nothing is a gimmick that wears thin: no costume theme, no novelty textures, no mascot.\n\nOne system at three volumes. The big screen is loudest: display type, the podium race and confetti. The voter's phone is medium: big tap targets and one moment of delight when a vote is in. Host views are quiet: the same colours and type, with nothing playful in the controls. The show screens carry no AwardBro branding; they belong to the people in the room.\n\nThere are two themes from one set of roles. **Night** (dark) is the default, because most shows happen in the evening in a dim room. **Paper** (light) is the same system on warm paper for daytime rooms and bright projectors. The big screen's theme is set by the host per show; phones and host views follow the device setting, with an override.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Rounded everything: Fredoka type, pill buttons, rounded-top podium columns.",
      "Solid, saturated colour that survives a washed-out projector; no glows or gradients.",
      "Results as a podium race: columns rise, each nomination in its own colour, the leader stalls, the winner turns gold and lands.",
      "A small shape set (circle, triangle, squiggle) as markers and confetti, nothing more.",
      "Soft coloured shadows; never hard offset shadows."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Gold Is Earned Rule",
        "body": "The winner colour belongs to the winner alone: never a button, never a runner-up's column. Nothing else on the reveal is gold (or Podium Coral on Paper), so the moment it appears, the room knows.",
